; TARN'S LANDING (Phase 38N2) — the fishing hamlet on the western water, and the realm's THIRD market.
;
; Hana the fishmonger has named it since 38L ("Tarn's Landing sends what it can, when the road lets
; it"). It is the Emberdeep Mine's mirror: a place with one thing in abundance and a need for
; everything else. Wenna Tarn sells fish at a markup nobody up the hill can match; Odger Vane pays
; over the odds for rope, cloth and iron and ⚠️ WILL NOT BUY FISH — the refusal is the design, and it
; is what stops a third settlement being a third stall (38N1's finding, now a step in the recipe).
;
; ⚠️ THE WATER IS A DECAL, NOT A VOLUME. A translucent plane 5 cm above the floor with NO COLLIDER,
; and the floor collider runs on underneath it. Swimming does not exist (Phase 39C owns traversal
; verbs), so a real water volume would be either an invisible wall or a hole to fall in. This way the
; shoreline reads, the player can wade, and nothing has to be built to support it.
;
; ⚠️ The dock and the jetties are built to stand IN water: their posts run below their own origin
; (dock min.y = -2.35, jetty min.y = -1.05), measured off the written .glb. The jetties are therefore
; sunk 0.30 m so their decks land flush at +0.04 rather than as a 34 cm kerb — CharacterBody3D has no
; step-up (38K), and a deck you catch your feet on is worse than a deck you walk over.
;
; ⚠️ Cell placed at Center (-106, 0, -10), abutting wilds_west's 50 m floor which ends at x = -80: a
; 52 m floor centred at x = -106 starts exactly there. Every transform here is LOCAL. The road in is
; from the EAST, so local +x is toward the valley and the water is west.
;
; ⚠️ EVERYTHING STATIC PARENTS TO Nav; the two merchants deliberately do not (only static geometry
; should carve the navmesh).
;
; ⚠️ WHAT THE 2026-08-28 LAYOUT REBUILD REPLACED, AND ONE OF IT WAS A BUG. The cell was four east-west bands: road, hamlet,
; shingle, and a 20 m strip of tarn down the whole western edge. Two problems. It read as a diagram —
; every building on one line beside one track — and the water covered the ENTIRE western seam, which
; is where wilds_west meets this cell at local (-26, 0). There was no walkable ground between the two
; cells at all, and nothing anywhere says so.
;
; THE LAYOUT NOW — a shore road the hamlet is NOT on, and a spit it is:
;   z -10..-1     THE SHORE ROAD, in from the town seam at local z = -8 (world z = -14, which is where
;                 town_hub's west spur leaves) and west along the bay's north edge to the wilds_west
;                 seam at local z = 0. Both seams are now dry ground.
;   x 4..18,      THE CHANDLER'S YARD, north of the road: Odger's chandlery, the carts, the cordage
;   z -20..-8     and the waystone. The trading half, and the only part visible from the road.
;   (-6, -2..4)   THE NECK — six metres wide, the only way down onto the spit.
;   x -15..1,     THE SPIT. Wenna's curing hut and six drying racks, the shore fire, the dock complex
;   z 2..14       standing off its south tip and Elyndra's shrine facing the water at its west point.
;                 The bay wraps it on three sides.
;   x -26..-16    THE WEST ARM of the tarn, z -6..26, with the west jetty running out into it.
;   x -16..2      THE SOUTH ARM, z 14..26, with the south jetty and the dock complex.
;
; ⚠️ THE WATER IS TWO VISUAL BOXES AND HAS NO COLLIDER, which is the convention this cell already
; used: Lakebed/Tarn (and now LakebedSouth/TarnSouth) are MeshInstance3Ds parented OUTSIDE Nav at
; y = 0.02 / 0.05 over the same flat 52 m floor everything else stands on. The player can walk on the
; tarn. That was true before this rebuild too; it is greybox, not a regression.
;
; ⚠️ EVERYTHING STATIC PARENTS TO Nav. Geometry outside the NavigationRegion3D is not carved into the
; navmesh. The two merchants deliberately do not.

[sub_resource type="NavigationMesh" id="NavMesh_tarn"]
geometry_parsed_geometry_type = 1
cell_size = 0.25
cell_height = 0.25
agent_height = 1.75
agent_radius = 0.5
agent_max_climb = 0.5

[sub_resource type="BoxMesh" id="BoxMesh_floor"]
size = Vector3(52, 0.5, 52)

[sub_resource type="BoxShape3D" id="Shape_floor"]
size = Vector3(52, 0.5, 52)

; Wet grey-brown shingle, colder than the mine's spoil and the square's packed earth.
[sub_resource type="StandardMaterial3D" id="Mat_floor"]
albedo_color = Color(0.29, 0.29, 0.27, 1)
roughness = 0.94

; The shore path — the one lighter surface, so the route from the road to the water is legible.
[sub_resource type="StandardMaterial3D" id="Mat_shore"]
albedo_color = Color(0.42, 0.4, 0.36, 1)
roughness = 0.9

; THE TARN. Transparency = 1 is ALPHA blending; the alpha in albedo_color is what makes the shingle
; read through the shallows. No collider anywhere near it — see the header note.
[sub_resource type="StandardMaterial3D" id="Mat_water"]
transparency = 1
albedo_color = Color(0.1, 0.26, 0.3, 0.82)
metallic = 0.35
roughness = 0.08

; ⚠️ The first pass had water at alpha 0.62 over the SAME shingle the shore is made of, and at eye
; level it read as flat grey ground — a transparent surface needs something dark underneath it to be
; transparent against. This is the lakebed: a near-black skin under the tarn, no collider, so the
; shallows read as depth and the waterline reads as an edge.
[sub_resource type="StandardMaterial3D" id="Mat_lakebed"]
albedo_color = Color(0.09, 0.11, 0.12, 1)
roughness = 0.98

; The 2026-08-28 layout rebuild: the tarn is an L-shaped BAY in two boxes rather than one 20 m band down the west edge.
; The band was why nothing could walk from wilds_west into this cell — the whole western seam was
; water. The bay now leaves a shore road along the north, and the land it wraps is the spit.
[sub_resource type="BoxMesh" id="BoxMesh_water_west"]
size = Vector3(10, 0.05, 32)

[sub_resource type="BoxMesh" id="BoxMesh_water_south"]
size = Vector3(18, 0.05, 12)

